 ## Notes
 
 助けて！ (たすけて！) means "Help!" The て-form here requests assistance.
+佐 and 助 overlap in assistance-related glosses: 佐 usually points to an aide or assistant, especially in compounds such as 補佐; 助 is the broader everyday character for helping or rescuing.
 Do not confuse the left-hand 且 with the 田 above 力 in [男](男.md).
